Frida Kahlo (1907–1934) was a pioneering Mexican artist, writer, poet, and filmmaker, widely regarded as one of the most influential figures in modern art, particularly in Latin America. Her work, marked by intense emotional expression, surrealism, and introspection, remains a cornerstone of contemporary visual arts.

